On the twenty-seventh day of my internship, I continued studying 
networking with a focus on SSH. Since I had previously used SSH to 
connect to the OverTheWire Bandit server, I wanted to understand
the technology behind the connection in more detail.

I studied the basic difference between public and private keys 
and learned how SSH keys can be used for authentication. 
I also read about the scp command and how it can be used to 
transfer files between systems.

I continued working on the Bandit challenges and reviewed 
my previous SSH experience. This helped me understand that 
SSH is not only a tool for completing the Bandit exercises 
but also an important method for remotely managing Linux systems.
